DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The tteeee node type has a purpose similar to the tee(1) command.  TTeeee nodes
     are useful for debugging or “snooping” on a connection between two net‐
     graph nodes.  TTeeee nodes have four hooks, right, left, right2left, and
     left2right.  All data received on right is sent unmodified to _b_o_t_h hooks
     left and right2left.  Similarly, all data received on left is sent unmod‐
     ified to both right and left2right.

     Packets may also be received on right2left and left2right; if so, they
     are forwarded unchanged out hooks right and left, respectively.

HHOOOOKKSS
     This node type supports the following hooks:

     _r_i_g_h_t       The connection to the node on the right.

     _l_e_f_t        The connection to the node on the left.

     _r_i_g_h_t_2_l_e_f_t  Tap for right to left traffic.

     _l_e_f_t_2_r_i_g_h_t  Tap for left to right traffic.

CCOONNTTRROOLL MMEESSSSAAGGEESS
     This node type supports the generic control messages, plus the following.

     NGM_TEE_GET_STATS (ggeettssttaattss)
          Get statistics, returned as a struct ng_tee_stats.

     NGM_TEE_CLR_STATS (ccllrrssttaattss)
          Clear statistics.

SSHHUUTTDDOOWWNN
     This node shuts down upon receipt of an NGM_SHUTDOWN control message, or
     when all hooks have been disconnected.  If both right and left hooks are
     present, node removes itself from the chain gently, connecting right and
     left together.

